# Jak 3, 0.1.8 (LIST-0.1.8 item 6, Steer by grabbing the wheel), run with JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=wasdoors-desert-turtle
# JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1: the desert buggy as jak3_buggy.sim starts in it. Driving (A: Cross, the throttle), both grips
# squeezed with the hands where they rest (the wheel held), turned to the right as a wheel (the right down, the left
# up), back, let go; then the right grip's quick squeeze on the wheel (R2), squeezed again and held (R2 held: the
# turbo), and let go; both hands on it again, the right stick's click held (R2 held: the turbo with both hands on the
# wheel, "... the right stick's click with that hand on the wheel: R2"), and the wheel tilted back as a car's turned
# right (the right down and back, the left up and ahead). Expect "[vr-pad] the wheel ..." lines ("a wheel") and the
# buggy turning in the pictures.
# 0.1.8 (sim wh3, build 101): the continue seats Jak at about frame 4700, so the driving starts at 4900 (it began at
# 4500, and the first grab and turn came before he sat).
# Build 104 on: run with QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000 as well. The driving counts from the frame the continue seats him
# (pc-vr.gc vr-test-continue!, "[vr] test: seated by the continue, the set-up done"), 60 frames after it.
